ce_University.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"190" height=3D"276" style=3D=
"--mw-file-upright: 0.75" class=3D"mw-file-element mw-file-upright" data-fi=
le-width=3D"2034" data-file-height=3D"2954"></a><figcaption>President <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_F._Kennedy" title=3D"John F. Kenne=
dy">John F. Kennedy</a> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/We_choose_=
to_go_to_the_Moon" title=3D"We choose to go to the Moon">speaking at Rice U=
niversity</a> on September 12, 1962</figcaption></figure>
<p>In spite of that, the proposed program faced widespread opposition and w=
as dubbed a "<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boondoggle" title=3D"=
Boondoggle">moondoggle</a>" by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nor=
bert_Wiener" title=3D"Norbert Wiener">Norbert Wiener</a>, a mathematician a=
t the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massachusetts_Institute_of_T=
echnology" title=3D"Massachusetts Institute of Technology">Massachusetts In=
stitute of Technology</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-26" class=3D"reference"><a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-26"><span class=3D"=
cite-bracket">[</span>26<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-27" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-27"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>27<span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The effort to land a man on the M=
oon already had a name: <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Ap=
ollo" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Project Apollo">Project Apollo</a>.<su=
p id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson197915_28-0" class=3D"referen=
ce"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBr=
ooksGrimwoodSwenson197915-28"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>28<span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> When Kennedy met with <a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikita_Khrushchev" title=3D"Nikita Khrushchev=
">Nikita Khrushchev</a>, the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premi=
er_of_the_Soviet_Union" title=3D"Premier of the Soviet Union">Premier of th=
e Soviet Union</a> in June 1961, he proposed making the Moon landing a join=
t project, but Khrushchev declined the offer.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTELo=
gsdon201132_29-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTELogsdon201132-29"><span class=3D"cite-brack=
et">[</span>29<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Kennedy again=
 proposed a joint expedition to the Moon in a speech to the <a href=3D"http=
s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_General_Assembly" title=3D"United =
Nations General Assembly">United Nations General Assembly</a> on September =
20, 1963.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-30" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-30"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</=
span>30<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The idea of a joint =
Moon mission was ultimately abandoned after Kennedy's death.<sup id=3D"cite=
_ref-31" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apoll=
o_11#cite_note-31"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>31<span class=3D"ci=
te-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>An early and crucial decision was choosing <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_orbit_rendezvous" title=3D"Lunar orbit rendezvous">lu=
nar orbit rendezvous</a> over both <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Direct_ascent" title=3D"Direct ascent">direct ascent</a> and <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth_orbit_rendezvous" title=3D"Earth orbit re=
ndezvous">Earth orbit rendezvous</a>. A <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Space_rendezvous" title=3D"Space rendezvous">space rendezvous</a> is =
an <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orbital_maneuver" title=3D"Orbi=
tal maneuver">orbital maneuver</a> in which two spacecraft navigate through=
 space and meet up. In July 1962, NASA head <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/James_E._Webb" title=3D"James E. Webb">James Webb</a> announced t=
hat lunar orbit rendezvous would be used<sup id=3D"cite_ref-32" class=3D"re=
ference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-32"><=
span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>32<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span>=
</a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESwensonGrimwoodAlexander196685=E2=80=
=9386_33-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ap=
ollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTESwensonGrimwoodAlexander196685%E2%80%9386-33"><sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>33<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></=
a></sup> and that the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_(spac=
ecraft)" title=3D"Apollo (spacecraft)">Apollo spacecraft</a> would have thr=
ee major parts: a command module (CM) with a cabin for the three astronauts=
, and the only part that returned to Earth; a service module (SM), which su=
pported the command module with propulsion, electrical power, oxygen, and w=
ater; and a lunar module (LM) that had two stages=E2=80=94a descent stage f=
or landing on the Moon, and an ascent stage to place the astronauts back in=
to lunar orbit.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson197972=E2=
=80=9377_34-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson197972%E2%80%9377-34"><sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>34<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></=
a></sup> This design meant the spacecraft could be launched by a single <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturn_V" title=3D"Saturn V">Saturn V=
</a> rocket that was then under development.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBro=
oksGrimwoodSwenson197948=E2=80=9349_35-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwens=
on197948%E2%80%9349-35"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>35<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Technologies and techniques required for Apollo were developed by <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Gemini" title=3D"Project Gem=
ini">Project Gemini</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson19=
79181=E2=80=93182,_205=E2=80=93208_36-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenso=
n1979181%E2%80%93182,_205%E2%80%93208-36"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</s=
pan>36<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The Apollo project wa=
s enabled by NASA's adoption of new advances in <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Semiconductor_device" title=3D"Semiconductor device">semicond=
uctor device</a>, including <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal%=
E2%80%93oxide%E2%80%93semiconductor_field-effect_transistor" class=3D"mw-re=
direct" title=3D"Metal=E2=80=93oxide=E2=80=93semiconductor field-effect tra=
nsistor">metal=E2=80=93oxide=E2=80=93semiconductor field-effect transistors=
</a> (MOSFETs) in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interplaneta=
ry_Monitoring_Platform" title=3D"Interplanetary Monitoring Platform">Interp=
lanetary Monitoring Platform</a> (IMP)<sup id=3D"cite_ref-37" class=3D"refe=
rence"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-37"><sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>37<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></=
a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-38" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-38"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</s=
pan>38<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silicon" title=3D"Silicon">silicon</a> <a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_circuit" title=3D"Integrated circui=
t">integrated circuit</a> (IC) chips in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Apollo_Guidance_Computer" title=3D"Apollo Guidance Computer">Apol=
lo Guidance Computer</a> (AGC).<sup id=3D"cite_ref-39" class=3D"reference">=
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-39"><span clas=
s=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>39<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup=
>
</p><p>Project Apollo was abruptly halted by the <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/Apollo_1" title=3D"Apollo 1">Apollo 1</a> fire on January 27=
, 1967, in which astronauts <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gus_Gr=
issom" title=3D"Gus Grissom">Gus Grissom</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Ed_White_(astronaut)" title=3D"Ed White (astronaut)">Ed White</=
a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_B._Chaffee" title=3D=
"Roger B. Chaffee">Roger B. Chaffee</a> died, and the subsequent investigat=
ion.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979214=E2=80=93218_40=
-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#=
cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979214%E2%80%93218-40"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>40<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>=
 In October 1968, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_7" title=
=3D"Apollo 7">Apollo 7</a> evaluated the command module in Earth orbit,<sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979265=E2=80=93272_41-0" clas=
s=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_not=
e-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979265%E2%80%93272-41"><span class=3D"cite-=
bracket">[</span>41<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and in D=
ecember <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_8" title=3D"Apollo =
8">Apollo 8</a> tested it in lunar orbit.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooks=
GrimwoodSwenson1979274=E2=80=93284_42-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenso=
n1979274%E2%80%93284-42"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>42<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> In March 1969, <a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_9" title=3D"Apollo 9">Apollo 9</a> put the lunar m=
odule through its paces in Earth orbit,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGr=
imwoodSwenson1979292=E2=80=93300_43-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1=
979292%E2%80%93300-43"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>43<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and in May <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Apollo_10" title=3D"Apollo 10">Apollo 10</a> conducted a "dre=
ss rehearsal" in lunar orbit. By July 1969, all was in readiness for Apollo=
 11 to take the final step onto the Moon.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooks=
GrimwoodSwenson1979303=E2=80=93312_44-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenso=
n1979303%E2%80%93312-44"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>44<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>The Soviet Union appeared to be winning the Space Race, but its earl=
y lead was overtaken by the US <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro=
ject_Gemini" title=3D"Project Gemini">Gemini program</a> and Soviet failure=
 to develop the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N1_(rocket)" title=
=3D"N1 (rocket)">N1 launcher</a>, which would have been comparable to the S=
aturn V.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-45" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-45"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</s=
pan>45<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Seeing these failures=
, the Soviets then attempted to beat the US to return lunar material to the=
 Earth by means of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncrewed_spacec=
raft" title=3D"Uncrewed spacecraft">uncrewed probes</a>. On July 13, three =
days before Apollo 11's launch, the Soviet Union launched <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luna_15" title=3D"Luna 15">Luna 15</a>, which reach=
ed lunar orbit before Apollo 11. During descent, a malfunction caused Luna =
15 to crash in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mare_Crisium" title=
=3D"Mare Crisium">Mare Crisium</a> about two hours before Armstrong and Ald=
rin took off from the Moon's surface to return to earth. The <a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuffield_Radio_Astronomy_Laboratories" class=3D"=
mw-redirect" title=3D"Nuffield Radio Astronomy Laboratories">Nuffield Radio=
 Astronomy Laboratories</a> radio telescope in England recorded transmissio=
ns from Luna 15 during its descent, and these were released in July 2009 fo=
r the 40th anniversary of Apollo 11.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-46" class=3D"refere=
nce"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-46"><span=
 class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>46<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a>=
</sup>
</p>
