<p>The initial crew assignment of Commander <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Neil_Armstrong" title=3D"Neil Armstrong">Neil Armstrong</a>, Comm=
and Module Pilot (CMP) <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Lovell"=
 title=3D"Jim Lovell">Jim Lovell</a>, and Lunar Module Pilot (LMP) <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzz_Aldrin" title=3D"Buzz Aldrin">Buzz A=
ldrin</a> on the backup crew for Apollo&nbsp;9 was officially announced on =
November 20, 1967.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979374_=
47-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_1=
1#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979374-47"><span class=3D"cite-br=
acket">[</span>47<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Lovell and=
 Aldrin had previously flown together as the crew of <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Gemini_12" title=3D"Gemini 12">Gemini 12</a>. Due to des=
ign and manufacturing delays in the LM, Apollo&nbsp;8 and Apollo&nbsp;9 swa=
pped prime and backup crews, and Armstrong's crew became the backup for Apo=
llo&nbsp;8. Based on the normal crew rotation scheme, Armstrong was then ex=
pected to command Apollo 11.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHansen2005312=E2=80=
=93313_48-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A=
pollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHansen2005312%E2%80%93313-48"><span class=3D"cit=
e-bracket">[</span>48<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>There would be one change. <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Michael_Collins_(astronaut)" title=3D"Michael Collins (astronaut)">Michael =
Collins</a>, the CMP on the Apollo&nbsp;8 crew, began experiencing trouble =
with his legs. Doctors diagnosed a bony growth between his fifth and sixth =
vertebrae, requiring surgery.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECollins2001288=E2=
=80=93289_49-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECollins2001288%E2%80%93289-49"><span class=3D=
"cite-bracket">[</span>49<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Lo=
vell took his place on the Apollo&nbsp;8 crew, and when Collins recovered h=
e joined Armstrong's crew as CMP. In the meantime, <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Fred_Haise" title=3D"Fred Haise">Fred Haise</a> filled in =
as backup LMP, and Aldrin as backup CMP for Apollo 8.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FO=
OTNOTECunningham2010109_50-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECunningham2010109-50"><span cla=
ss=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>50<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></su=
p> Apollo 11 was the second American mission where all the crew members had=
 prior spaceflight experience,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEOrloff200090_51-0=
" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#ci=
te_note-FOOTNOTEOrloff200090-51"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>51<sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> the first being Apollo 10.<sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEOrloff200072_52-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEOrloff200072-52"><=
span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>52<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span>=
</a></sup> The next was <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STS-26" ti=
tle=3D"STS-26">STS-26</a> in 1988.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEOrloff200090_=
51-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_1=
1#cite_note-FOOTNOTEOrloff200090-51"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>5=
1<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deke_Slayton" title=3D"Deke=
 Slayton">Deke Slayton</a> gave Armstrong the option to replace Aldrin with=
 Lovell, since some thought Aldrin was difficult to work with. Armstrong ha=
d no issues working with Aldrin but thought it over for a day before declin=
ing. He thought Lovell deserved to command his own mission (eventually <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_13" title=3D"Apollo 13">Apollo =
13</a>).<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHansen2005338=E2=80=93339_53-0" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-FOOTNOTEHansen2005338%E2%80%93339-53"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span=
>53<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>The Apollo 11 prime crew had none of the close cheerful camaraderie =
characterized by that of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_12=
" title=3D"Apollo 12">Apollo 12</a>. Instead, they forged an amiable workin=
g relationship. Armstrong in particular was notoriously aloof, but Collins,=
 who considered himself a loner, confessed to rebuffing Aldrin's attempts t=
o create a more personal relationship.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECollins20=
01434=E2=80=93435_54-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECollins2001434%E2%80%93435-54"><span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>54<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a><=
/sup> Aldrin and Collins described the crew as "amiable strangers".<sup id=
=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHansen2005359_55-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHansen2005359-55"><s=
pan class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>55<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span><=
/a></sup> Armstrong did not agree with the assessment, and said "all the cr=
ews I was on worked very well together."<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHansen2=
005359_55-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A=
pollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHansen2005359-55"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[=
</span>55<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Backup_crew">Backup crew</h=
3></div>
