<p>The backup crew consisted of Lovell as Commander, <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Anders" title=3D"William Anders">William Anders<=
/a> as CMP, and Haise as LMP. Anders had flown with Lovell on Apollo&nbsp;8=
.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEOrloff200090_51-2" class=3D"reference"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEOrloff200090-=
51"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>51<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</=
span></a></sup> In early 1969, Anders accepted a job with the <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Space_Council" title=3D"National Space=
 Council">National Aeronautics and Space Council</a> effective August 1969,=
 and announced he would retire as an astronaut at that time. <a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Mattingly" title=3D"Ken Mattingly">Ken Matti=
ngly</a> was moved from the support crew into parallel training with Anders=
 as backup CMP in case Apollo 11 was delayed past its intended July launch =
date, at which point Anders would be unavailable.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNO=
TESlaytonCassutt1994237_56-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTESlaytonCassutt1994237-56"><span=
 class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>56<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a>=
</sup>
</p><p>Under the normal Apollo crew rotation, Lovell, Mattingly, and Haise =
would have been assigned to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo=
_14" title=3D"Apollo 14">Apollo 14</a>. However, because <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Shepard" title=3D"Alan Shepard">Alan Shepard</a=
> had only recently returned to flight status and needed additional trainin=
g, NASA reassigned his crew to Apollo 14 and moved Lovell's crew up to fly =
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_13" title=3D"Apollo 13">Apo=
llo 13</a> instead.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-58" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-58"><span class=3D"cite-br=
acket">[</span>a<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Shortly bef=
ore launch, Mattingly was replaced by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Jack_Swigert" title=3D"Jack Swigert">Jack Swigert</a> due to concerns o=
ver possible measles exposure.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESlaytonCassutt199=
4237_56-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apo=
llo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTESlaytonCassutt1994237-56"><span class=3D"cite-brac=
ket">[</span>56<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Support_crew">Support crew<=
/h3></div>
<p>During Projects Mercury and Gemini, each mission had a prime and a backu=
p crew. For Apollo, NASA added a third group, the support crew. Their job w=
as to maintain the flight plan, checklists, and mission rules, and to keep =
the prime and backup crews updated on any changes. They also developed proc=
edures=E2=80=94especially for emergencies, so that by the time the prime an=
d backup crews entered the simulators, they could focus on practicing and m=
astering them.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979261_59-0=
" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#ci=
te_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979261-59"><span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">[</span>58<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The support cr=
ew for Apollo 11 was Mattingly, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ro=
nald_Evans_(astronaut)" title=3D"Ronald Evans (astronaut)">Ronald Evans</a>=
, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_R._Pogue" class=3D"m=
w-redirect" title=3D"William R. Pogue">Bill Pogue</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-F=
OOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979375_60-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwens=
on1979375-60"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>59<span class=3D"cite-br=
acket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Capsule_communicators">Caps=
ule communicators</h3></div>
<figure class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File/Thumb"><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Duke,_Lovell_and_Haise_at_the_Apollo_11_Capco=
m,_Johnson_Space_Center,_Houston,_Texas_-_19690720.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-de=
scription"><img src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb=
/5/5d/Duke%2C_Lovell_and_Haise_at_the_Apollo_11_Capcom%2C_Johnson_Space_Cen=
ter%2C_Houston%2C_Texas_-_19690720.jpg/250px-Duke%2C_Lovell_and_Haise_at_th=
e_Apollo_11_Capcom%2C_Johnson_Space_Center%2C_Houston%2C_Texas_-_19690720.j=
pg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"250" height=3D"168" class=3D"mw-file-elemen=
t" data-file-width=3D"4132" data-file-height=3D"2784"></a><figcaption>CAPCO=
M <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Duke" title=3D"Charles D=
uke">Charles Duke</a> (left), with backup crewmembers Lovell and Haise list=
ening in during Apollo 11's descent</figcaption></figure>
<p>The <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capsule_communicator" class=
=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Capsule communicator">capsule communicator</a> (C=
APCOM) was an astronaut stationed at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Christopher_C._Kraft_Jr._Mission_Control_Center" title=3D"Christophe=
r C. Kraft Jr. Mission Control Center">Mission Control Center</a> in <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houston" title=3D"Houston">Houston</a>, =
Texas, and was typically the only person permitted to communicate directly =
with the flight crew.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKranz200027_61-0" class=3D=
"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FO=
OTNOTEKranz200027-61"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>60<span class=3D=
"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> This practice ensured that messages came =
from someone best able to understand the situation in the spacecraft and to=
 relay guidance from <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flight_contro=
ller" title=3D"Flight controller">flight controllers</a> as clearly as poss=
ible. For Apollo 11, the CAPCOMs were backup and support crew members Ander=
s, Evans, Haise, Lovell, and Mattingly, along with <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Duke" title=3D"Charles Duke">Charles Duke</a>, <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owen_Garriott" title=3D"Owen Garriott=
">Owen Garriott</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Don_L._Lind" =
class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Don L. Lind">Don L. Lind</a>, <a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_McCandless_II" title=3D"Bruce McCandless I=
I">Bruce McCandless II</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ha=
rrison_Schmitt" title=3D"Harrison Schmitt">Harrison Schmitt</a>.<sup id=3D"=
cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979375_60-1" class=3D"reference"><a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGri=
mwoodSwenson1979375-60"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>59<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
