</p><p>Weather satellites were not yet common, but US Air Force <a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Captain_(United_States_O-3)" title=3D"Captain=
 (United States O-3)">Captain</a> Hank Brandli had access to top-secret <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CORONA_(satellite)" title=3D"CORONA (=
satellite)">spy satellite</a> images. He realized that a storm front was he=
aded for the Apollo recovery area. Poor visibility which could make locatin=
g the capsule difficult, and strong upper-level winds which "would have rip=
ped their parachutes to shreds" according to Brandli, posed a serious threa=
t to the safety of the mission.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-194" class=3D"reference"=
><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-194"><span cl=
ass=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>192<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></=
sup> Brandli alerted Navy Captain Willard S. Houston Jr., the commander of =
the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joint_Typhoon_Warning_Center" =
title=3D"Joint Typhoon Warning Center">Fleet Weather Center</a> at Pearl Ha=
rbor, who had the required security clearance. On their recommendation, <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rear_admiral_(United_States)" title=
=3D"Rear admiral (United States)">Rear Admiral</a> <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Donald_C._Davis" title=3D"Donald C. Davis">Donald C. Davis=
</a>, commander of Manned Spaceflight Recovery Forces, Pacific, advised NAS=
A to change the recovery area, each man risking his career. A new location =
was selected 215 nautical miles (398&nbsp;km) northeast.<sup id=3D"cite_ref=
-ALSJ_Re-entry_195-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-ALSJ_Re-entry-195"><span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
>[</span>193<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_=
ref-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010136=E2=80=93137,_144=E2=80=93145_196-0" class=3D"=
reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOO=
TNOTECarmichael2010136%E2%80%93137,_144%E2%80%93145-196"><span class=3D"cit=
e-bracket">[</span>194<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>This altered the flight plan. A different sequence of computer progr=
ams was used, one never before attempted. In a conventional entry, trajecto=
ry event P64 was followed by P67. For a skip-out re-entry, P65 and P66 were=
 employed to handle the exit and entry parts of the skip. In this case, bec=
ause they were extending the re-entry but not actually skipping out, P66 wa=
s not invoked and instead, P65 led directly to P67. The crew were also warn=
ed they would not be in a full-lift (heads-down) attitude when they entered=
 P67.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-ALSJ_Re-entry_195-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-ALSJ_Re-entry-195"><s=
pan class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>193<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span>=
</a></sup> The first program's acceleration subjected the astronauts to 6.5=
 standard gravities (64&nbsp;m/s<sup>2</sup>); the second, to 6.0 standard =
gravities (59&nbsp;m/s<sup>2</sup>).<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMission_Eva=
luation_Team196928_197-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team196928-197">=
<span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>195<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</spa=
n></a></sup>
</p><p>Before dawn on July 24, <i>Hornet</i> launched four Sea King helicop=
ters and three <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grumman_E-1_Tracer"=
 title=3D"Grumman E-1 Tracer">Grumman E-1 Tracers</a>. Two of the E-1s were=
 designated as "air boss" while the third acted as a communications relay a=
ircraft. Two of the Sea Kings carried divers and recovery equipment. The th=
ird carried photographic equipment, and the fourth carried the decontaminat=
ion swimmer and the flight surgeon.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMission_Eval=
uation_Team1969169=E2=80=93170_198-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team=
1969169%E2%80%93170-198"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>196<span clas=
s=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> At 16:44 UTC (05:44 local time) <i>Co=
lumbia</i><span class=3D"nowrap" style=3D"padding-left:0.1em;">'</span>s <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drogue_parachute" title=3D"Drogue pa=
rachute">drogue parachutes</a> were deployed. This was observed by the heli=
copters. Seven minutes later <i>Columbia</i> struck the water forcefully 2,=
660&nbsp;km (1,440&nbsp;nmi) east of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Wake_Island" title=3D"Wake Island">Wake Island</a>, 380&nbsp;km (210&nbs=
p;nmi) south of Johnston Atoll, and 24&nbsp;km (13&nbsp;nmi) from <i>Hornet=
</i>,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEOrloff2000109_9-4" class=3D"reference"><a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEOrloff200=
0109-9"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>9<span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-ALSJ_Re-entry_195-2" class=3D"referen=
ce"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-ALSJ_Re-en=
try-195"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>193<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">]</span></a></sup> at <span class=3D"geo-inline"><link rel=3D"mw-dedupli=
cated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1156832818"><span class=
=3D"plainlinks nourlexpansion"><span style=3D"position: relative; white-spa=
