te-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>During <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splashdown" title=3D=
"Splashdown">splashdown</a>, <i>Columbia</i> landed upside down but was rig=
hted within ten minutes by flotation bags activated by the astronauts.<sup =
id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team1969164=E2=80=93167_202-0" cl=
ass=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_n=
ote-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team1969164%E2%80%93167-202"><span class=3D"=
cite-bracket">[</span>200<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> A =
diver from the Navy helicopter hovering above attached a <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_anchor" title=3D"Sea anchor">sea anchor</a> to p=
revent it from drifting.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010184=E2=80=
=93185_203-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010184%E2%80%93185-203"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>201<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup=
> More divers attached flotation collars to stabilize the module and positi=
oned rafts for astronaut extraction.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECarmichael2=
010186=E2=80=93188_204-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010186%E2%80%93188-204">=
<span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>202<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</spa=
n></a></sup>
</p>
