<p>The divers then passed biological isolation garments (BIGs) to the astro=
nauts, and assisted them into the life raft. The possibility of bringing ba=
ck <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathogen" title=3D"Pathogen">pa=
thogens</a> from the lunar surface was considered remote, but NASA took pre=
cautions at the recovery site. The astronauts were rubbed down with a <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_hypochlorite" title=3D"Sodium hy=
pochlorite">sodium hypochlorite</a> solution and <i>Columbia</i> wiped with=
 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Povidone-iodine" title=3D"Povidon=
e-iodine">povidone-iodine</a> to remove any lunar dust that might be presen=
t. The astronauts were winched on board the recovery helicopter. BIGs were =
worn until they reached isolation facilities on board <i>Hornet</i>. The ra=
ft containing decontamination materials was intentionally sunk.<sup id=3D"c=
ite_ref-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team1969164=E2=80=93167_202-1" class=3D"=
reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOO=
TNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team1969164%E2%80%93167-202"><span class=3D"cite-br=
acket">[</span>200<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>After touchdown on <i>Hornet</i> at 17:53 UTC, the helicopter was lo=
wered by the elevator into the hangar bay, where the astronauts walked the =
30 feet (9.1&nbsp;m) to the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile=
_quarantine_facility" title=3D"Mobile quarantine facility">mobile quarantin=
e facility</a> (MQF), where they would begin the Earth-based portion of the=
ir 21 days of quarantine.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010199=E2=
=80=93200_205-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010199%E2%80%93200-205"><span cla=
ss=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>203<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></s=
up> This practice would continue for two more Apollo missions, Apollo 12 an=
d <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_14" title=3D"Apollo 14">A=
pollo 14</a>, before the Moon was proven to be barren of life, and the quar=
antine process dropped.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEJohnstonDietleinBerry197=
5406=E2=80=93424_206-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEJohnstonDietleinBerry1975406%E2%80%93=
424-206"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>204<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-207" class=3D"reference"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-207"><span class=3D"c=
ite-bracket">[</span>205<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Nix=
on welcomed the astronauts back to Earth. He told them: "[A]s a result of w=
hat you've done, the world has never been closer together before."<sup id=
=3D"cite_ref-208" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Apollo_11#cite_note-208"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>206<span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>After Nixon departed, <i>Hornet</i> was brought alongside the 5-shor=
t-ton (4.5&nbsp;t) <i>Columbia</i>, which was lifted aboard by the ship's c=
rane, placed on a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolly_(trailer)"=
 title=3D"Dolly (trailer)">dolly</a> and moved next to the MQF. It was then=
 attached to the MQF with a flexible tunnel, allowing the lunar samples, fi=
lm, data tapes and other items to be removed. <i>Hornet</i> returned to Pea=
rl Harbor, where the MQF was loaded onto a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Lockheed_C-141_Starlifter" title=3D"Lockheed C-141 Starlifter">Loc=
kheed C-141 Starlifter</a> and airlifted to the Manned Spacecraft Center. T=
he astronauts arrived at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar=
_Receiving_Laboratory" title=3D"Lunar Receiving Laboratory">Lunar Receiving=
 Laboratory</a> at 10:00 UTC on July 28. <i>Columbia</i> was taken to <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Island" title=3D"Ford Island">Ford=
 Island</a> for deactivation, and its pyrotechnics made safe. It was then t=
aken to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hickham_Air_Force_Base" cl=
ass=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Hickham Air Force Base">Hickham Air Force Base=
</a>, from whence it was flown to Houston in a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Douglas_C-133_Cargomaster" title=3D"Douglas C-133 Cargomaster"=
>Douglas C-133 Cargomaster</a>, reaching the Lunar Receiving Laboratory on =
July 30.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team1969166,_171=E2=
=80=93173_209-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMission_Evaluation_Team1969166,_171%E2%80%93=
173-209"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>207<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>In accordance with the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extr=
a-Terrestrial_Exposure_Law" title=3D"Extra-Terrestrial Exposure Law">Extra-=
Terrestrial Exposure Law</a>, a set of regulations promulgated by NASA on J=
uly 16 to codify its quarantine protocol,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-210" class=3D"=
reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-210=
"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>208<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</s=
pan></a></sup> the astronauts continued in quarantine. After three weeks in=
 confinement (first in the Apollo spacecraft, then in their trailer on <i>H=
ornet</i>, and finally in the Lunar Receiving Laboratory), the astronauts w=
ere given a clean bill of health.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-211" class=3D"referenc=
e"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-211"><span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>209<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a>=
</sup> On August 10, 1969, the Interagency Committee on Back Contamination =
met in Atlanta and lifted the quarantine on the astronauts, on those who ha=
d joined them in quarantine (NASA physician <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/William_Carpentier" title=3D"William Carpentier">William Carpenti=
er</a> and MQF project engineer <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jo=
hn_Hirasaki" title=3D"John Hirasaki">John Hirasaki</a>),<sup id=3D"cite_ref=
-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010118_212-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTECarmichael2010118-212"><spa=
n class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>210<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></=
a></sup> and on <i>Columbia</i> itself. Loose equipment from the spacecraft=
 remained in isolation until the lunar samples were released for study.<sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEErtelNewkirkBrooks1978312_213-0" class=3D"reference=
"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEErte=
lNewkirkBrooks1978312-213"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>211<span cl=
ass=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
