<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id=3D"Celebrations">Celebrations<=
/h2></div>
<p>Following their return to Earth, the Apollo 11 crew received widespread =
international acclaim. On August 13, 1969, astronauts <a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neil_Armstrong" title=3D"Neil Armstrong">Neil Armstrong=
</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzz_Aldrin" title=3D"Buzz A=
ldrin">Buzz Aldrin</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michae=
l_Collins_(astronaut)" title=3D"Michael Collins (astronaut)">Michael Collin=
s</a> were honored with ticker-tape parades in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/New_York_City" title=3D"New York City">New York City</a> and <=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago" title=3D"Chicago">Chicago<=
/a>, with an estimated six million people lining the streets.<sup id=3D"cit=
e_ref-nyc-chicago_214-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-nyc-chicago-214"><span class=3D"cite-bracket=
">[</span>212<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> In New York th=
e parade started at <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowling_Green_=
(New_York_City)" title=3D"Bowling Green (New York City)">Bowling Green</a> =
going down Broadway to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Ci=
ty_Hall" title=3D"New York City Hall">City Hall</a> where Mayor <a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Lindsay" title=3D"John Lindsay">John Lin=
dsay</a> greeted them and ended at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Headquarters_of_the_United_Nations" title=3D"Headquarters of the Unite=
d Nations">United Nations headquarters</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-215" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-215"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>213<span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
]</span></a></sup> Broadway was even temporarily renamed for that day to "A=
pollo Way". In Chicago the parade went to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Chicago_Loop" title=3D"Chicago Loop">the Loop</a><sup id=3D"cite_re=
f-216" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_=
11#cite_note-216"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>214<span class=3D"ci=
te-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and culminated at the <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_J._Daley_Center" title=3D"Richard J. Daley Cente=
r">Chicago Civic Center</a> where the astronauts and local officials spoke =
to the crowd. That evening, a state dinner was held in <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Los_Angeles" title=3D"Los Angeles">Los Angeles</a> at =
the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Century_Plaza_Hotel" class=3D"=
mw-redirect" title=3D"Century Plaza Hotel">Century Plaza Hotel</a> to comme=
morate the historic achievement. The event was attended by members of <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Congress" title=3D"United=
 States Congress">Congress</a>, 44 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Governor_(United_States)" title=3D"Governor (United States)">state governo=
rs</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_Justice_of_the_Unite=
d_States" title=3D"Chief Justice of the United States">Chief Justice of the=
 United States</a> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_E._Burge=
r" title=3D"Warren E. Burger">Warren E. Burger</a> and his predecessor <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earl_Warren" title=3D"Earl Warren">Ear=
l Warren</a>, as well as ambassadors from 83 nations. <a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_the_United_States" title=3D"President of t=
he United States">President</a> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ri=
chard_Nixon" title=3D"Richard Nixon">Richard Nixon</a> and <a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice_President_of_the_United_States" title=3D"Vice=
 President of the United States">Vice President</a> <a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Spiro_Agnew" title=3D"Spiro Agnew">Spiro Agnew</a> awarde=
d each astronaut the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidential_=
Medal_of_Freedom" title=3D"Presidential Medal of Freedom">Presidential Meda=
l of Freedom</a>, the highest civilian honor in the United States.<sup id=
=3D"cite_ref-state-dinner_217-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-state-dinner-217"><span class=3D"cit=
e-bracket">[</span>215<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<figure class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File/Thumb"><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:New_York_City_Welcomes_the_Apollo_11_Astronau=
ts_-_GPN-2002-000034.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https:/=
/upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/New_York_City_Welcomes_t=
he_Apollo_11_Astronauts_-_GPN-2002-000034.jpg/250px-New_York_City_Welcomes_=
the_Apollo_11_Astronauts_-_GPN-2002-000034.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D=
"250" height=3D"193" class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"2844" dat=
a-file-height=3D"2190"></a><figcaption>Apollo 11 Astronauts - New York City=
 - August 13, 1969</figcaption></figure>
<p>On September 16, the astronauts addressed a joint session of <a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Congress" title=3D"United State=
s Congress">Congress</a>, where they presented two <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_the_United_States" title=3D"Flag of the United Sta=
tes">American flags</a>=E2=80=94one to the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/United_States_House_of_Representatives" title=3D"United States Hou=
se of Representatives">House of Representatives</a> and one to the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Senate" title=3D"United Sta=
tes Senate">Senate</a>=E2=80=94that had traveled to the lunar surface aboar=
d <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_Lunar_Module" title=3D"Ap=
ollo Lunar Module">Eagle</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-congress-flag_218-0" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-congress-flag-218"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>216<span class=3D"=
cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>One of the mission flags carried aboard the flight=E2=80=94the <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_American_Samoa" title=3D"Flag o=
f American Samoa">Flag of American Samoa</a>=E2=80=94was later displayed at=
 the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_P._Haydon_Museum" title=
=3D"Jean P. Haydon Museum">Jean P. Haydon Museum</a> in <a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pago_Pago" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Pago Pago">=
Pago Pago</a>, the capital of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amer=
ican_Samoa" title=3D"American Samoa">American Samoa</a>, recognizing the te=
rritory's support role as a recovery staging area.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-samoa=
-flag_219-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A=
pollo_11#cite_note-samoa-flag-219"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>217=
<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<figure class=3D"mw-default-size mw-halign-left" typeof=3D"mw:File/Thumb"><=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_terrazzo.jpg" class=3D"=
mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com=
mons/thumb/e/ec/Apollo_terrazzo.jpg/250px-Apollo_terrazzo.jpg" decoding=3D"=
async" width=3D"250" height=3D"188" class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-wid=
th=3D"3264" data-file-height=3D"2448"></a><figcaption>Terrazzo tribute to A=
pollo 11 astronauts on the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollywo=
od_Walk_of_Fame" title=3D"Hollywood Walk of Fame">Hollywood Walk of Fame</a=
></figcaption></figure><p>Numerous countries and organizations honored the =
Moon landing by issuing special commemorative items. These included postage=
 stamps, coins, medals, plaques, and magazine features. <i><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_(magazine)" title=3D"Time (magazine)">TIME</a=
></i>, <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Geographic" tit=
le=3D"National Geographic">National Geographic</a></i>, <i><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_(magazine)" title=3D"Life (magazine)">LIFE</a=
></i>, and dozens of international publications featured the astronauts on =
their covers. Many of these commemoratives are now held in public and priva=
te collections, and some were placed aboard later Apollo missions in symbol=
ic tribute.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-commemoratives_220-0" class=3D"reference"><a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-commemoratives-2=
20"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>218<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]<=
/span></a></sup>
</p><p>Additionally, the success of Apollo 11 contributed to a brief spike =
in interest in science and technology education, often referred to as the "=
Apollo effect", influencing a generation of engineers and scientists.<sup i=
d=3D"cite_ref-apollo-effect_221-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-apollo-effect-221"><span class=3D"=
cite-bracket">[</span>219<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"World_tour">World tour</h3>=
</div>
<p>The celebrations continued with a 38-day world goodwill tour titled "Gia=
nt Leap", which began on September 29 and concluded on November 5, 1969. Th=
e astronauts visited 22 countries and met with numerous heads of state, pri=
me ministers, royalty, and civic leaders.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-world-tour_222=
-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#=
cite_note-world-tour-222"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>220<span cla=
ss=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The tour, intended to thank the inte=
rnational community for their support of the space program, began in <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexico_City" title=3D"Mexico City">Mexic=
o City</a> and ended in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo" tit=
le=3D"Tokyo">Tokyo</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-tour-start-end_223-0" class=3D"r=
eference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-tour=
-start-end-223"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>221<span class=3D"cite=
-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Notable stops included <a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Bogot%C3%A1" title=3D"Bogot=C3=A1">Bogot=C3=A1</a>, <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires" title=3D"Buenos Aires">Bu=
enos Aires</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_de_Janeiro" ti=
tle=3D"Rio de Janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Madrid" title=3D"Madrid">Madrid</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Paris" title=3D"Paris">Paris</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Amsterdam" title=3D"Amsterdam">Amsterdam</a>, <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brussels" title=3D"Brussels">Brussels</a>, <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London" title=3D"London">London</a>,<sup =
id=3D"cite_ref-tour-itinerary_224-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-tour-itinerary-224"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>222<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup=
> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Berlin" title=3D"West Berli=
n">West Berlin</a>,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-225" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-225"><span class=3D"cite-=
bracket">[</span>223<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome" title=3D"Rome">Rome</a>, <a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgrade" title=3D"Belgrade">Belgrade</a>, <=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tehran" title=3D"Tehran">Tehran</a>=
, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mumbai" title=3D"Mumbai">Mumbai<=
/a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangkok" title=3D"Bangkok">Ba=
ngkok</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sydney" title=3D"Sydney=
">Sydney</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guam" title=3D"Guam"=
>Guam</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honolulu" title=3D"=
Honolulu">Honolulu</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-tour-itinerary_224-1" class=3D"r=
eference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-tour=
-itinerary-224"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>222<span class=3D"cite=
-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Crowds in the tens or hundreds of thousands ga=
thered to greet the astronauts in each city.
</p><p>In London the astronauts went to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Buckingham_Palace" title=3D"Buckingham Palace">Buckingham Palace</a> =
were they were greeted by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabet=
h_II" title=3D"Elizabeth II">Queen Elizabeth II</a>. When they went to West=
 Berlin they were toured the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berli=
n_Wall" title=3D"Berlin Wall">Berlin Wall</a> by the city's mayor. When the=
y saw Belgrade were greeted by a crowd of between 400,000 and 500,000 peopl=
e from the airport to the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier where they placed a w=
reath and were welcomed to a luncheon by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Josip_Broz_Tito" title=3D"Josip Broz Tito">Josip Broz Tito</a>. When=
 they stopped in Kinshasa they received the National Order of the Leopard b=
y <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobutu_Sese_Seko" title=3D"Mobut=
u Sese Seko">Mobutu Sese Seko</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-226" class=3D"referen=
ce"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-226"><span=
 class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>224<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a=
></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id=3D"Legacy">Legacy</h2></div>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Cultural_significance">Cult=
ural significance</h3></div>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
1353705441"><div role=3D"note" class=3D"hatnote navigation-not-searchable">=
Main article: <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11_in_popular=
_culture" title=3D"Apollo 11 in popular culture">Apollo 11 in popular cultu=
re</a></div>
<figure class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File/Thumb"><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Land_on_the_Moon_7_21_1969-repair.jpg" class=
=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia=
/commons/thumb/9/9a/Land_on_the_Moon_7_21_1969-repair.jpg/250px-Land_on_the=
_Moon_7_21_1969-repair.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"250" height=3D"297"=
 class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"2356" data-file-height=3D"279=
5"></a><figcaption>A girl holding <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/The_Washington_Post" title=3D"The Washington Post">The Washington Post</=
a></i> newspaper stating <span style=3D"padding-right:.15em;">"</span>'The =
Eagle Has Landed' =E2=80=93 Two Men Walk on the Moon"</figcaption></figure>
<p>Humans walking on the Moon and returning safely to Earth accomplished Ke=
nnedy's goal set eight years earlier. In Mission Control during the Apollo =
11 landing, Kennedy's speech flashed on the screen, followed by the words "=
TASK ACCOMPLISHED, July 1969".<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Launius_227-0" class=3D"r=
eference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-Laun=
ius-227"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>225<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">]</span></a></sup> The success of Apollo 11 demonstrated the United Stat=
es' technological superiority;<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Launius_227-1" class=3D"r=
eference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-Laun=
ius-227"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>225<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">]</span></a></sup> and with the success of Apollo 11, America had won th=
e <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Race" title=3D"Space Race"=
>Space Race</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChaikin200757_228-0" class=3D"r=
eference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOT=
NOTEChaikin200757-228"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>226<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchefter199=
9288_229-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ap=
ollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchefter1999288-229"><span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
>[</span>227<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>New phrases permeated into the English language. "If they can send a=
 man to the Moon, why can't they&nbsp;...?" became a common saying followin=
g Apollo 11.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-230" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-230"><span class=3D"cite-bracket=
">[</span>228<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Armstrong's wo=
rds on the lunar surface also spun off various parodies.<sup id=3D"cite_ref=
-FOOTNOTEChaikin200757_228-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChaikin200757-228"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>226<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup=
>
</p><p>While most people celebrated the accomplishment, disenfranchised Ame=
ricans saw it as a symbol of the divide in America, evidenced by protesters=
 led by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Abernathy" title=3D"=
Ralph Abernathy">Ralph Abernathy</a> outside of Kennedy Space Center the da=
y before Apollo 11 launched.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchefter1999283_231=
-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#=
cite_note-FOOTNOTESchefter1999283-231"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span=
>229<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> NASA Administrator <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_O._Paine" title=3D"Thomas O. Pa=
ine">Thomas Paine</a> met with Abernathy at the occasion, both hoping that =
the space program can spur progress also in other regards, such as poverty =
in the US. Paine was then asked, and agreed, to host protesters as spectato=
rs at the launch, and Abernathy, awestruck by the spectacle,<sup id=3D"cite=
_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwoodSwenson1979338_106-1" class=3D"reference"><a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooksGrimwo=
odSwenson1979338-106"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>105<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> prayed for the astronauts.<sup id=3D"c=
ite_ref-Niiler_2019_232-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-Niiler_2019-232"><span class=3D"cite-brack=
et">[</span>230<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup class=3D=
"noprint Inline-Template noprint noexcerpt Template-Fact" style=3D"white-sp=
ace:nowrap;">[<i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifia=
bility#Questionable_sources" title=3D"Wikipedia:Verifiability"><span title=
