on"><img src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/4=
30-L1-S1_640.jpg/250px-430-L1-S1_640.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"250" =
height=3D"137" class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"2746" data-file=
-height=3D"1510"></a><figcaption>Pieces of fabric and wood from the first a=
irplane, the 1903 <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright_Flyer"=
 title=3D"Wright Flyer">Wright Flyer</a></i>, traveled to the Moon in Apoll=
o 11's <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Module_Eagle" title=
=3D"Lunar Module Eagle">Lunar Module <i>Eagle</i></a> and are displayed at =
the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wright_Brothers_National_Memor=
ial" title=3D"Wright Brothers National Memorial">Wright Brothers National M=
emorial</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Moon_rocks">Moon rocks</h3>=
</div>
<p>The main repository for the Apollo Moon rocks is the <a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Sample_Laboratory_Facility" title=3D"Lunar Samp=
le Laboratory Facility">Lunar Sample Laboratory Facility</a> at the Lyndon =
B. Johnson Space Center in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houston=
" title=3D"Houston">Houston</a>, Texas. For safekeeping, there is also a sm=
aller collection stored at <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_S=
ands_Test_Facility" title=3D"White Sands Test Facility">White Sands Test Fa=
cility</a> near <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Cruces,_New_Me=
xico" title=3D"Las Cruces, New Mexico">Las Cruces, New Mexico</a>. Most of =
the rocks are stored in nitrogen to keep them free of moisture. They are ha=
ndled only indirectly, using special tools. Over 100 research laboratories =
worldwide conduct studies of the samples; approximately 500 samples are pre=
pared and sent to investigators every year.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-259" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-259"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>257<span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-260" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-260"><span class=3D"cite-b=
racket">[</span>258<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>In November 1969, Nixon asked NASA to make up about 250 presentation=
 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11_lunar_sample_display" t=
itle=3D"Apollo 11 lunar sample display">Apollo 11 lunar sample displays</a>=
 for 135 nations, the fifty states of the United States and its possessions=
, and the United Nations. Each display included Moon dust from Apollo 11 an=
d flags, including one of the Soviet Union, taken along by Apollo 11. The r=
ice-sized particles were four small pieces of Moon soil weighing about 50&n=
bsp;mg and were enveloped in a clear acrylic button about as big as a <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half_dollar_(United_States_coin)" title=
=3D"Half dollar (United States coin)">United States half-dollar coin</a>. T=
his acrylic button magnified the grains of lunar dust. Nixon gave the Apoll=
o 11 lunar sample displays as goodwill gifts in 1970.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-26=
1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#c=
ite_note-261"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>259<span class=3D"cite-b=
racket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-262" class=3D"reference"><a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-262"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>260<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup=
>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Experiment_results">Experim=
ent results</h3></div>
<p>The Passive Seismic Experiment ran until the command uplink failed on Au=
gust 25, 1969. The downlink failed on December 14, 1969.<sup id=3D"cite_ref=
-FOOTNOTEBatesLauderdaleKernaghan19792-3_&amp;_4-32_263-0" class=3D"referen=
ce"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBa=
tesLauderdaleKernaghan19792-3_&amp;_4-32-263"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
[</span>261<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> As of 2018<sup c=
lass=3D"plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style=3D"display:none=
;"><a class=3D"external text" data-mw-original-href=3D"//en.wikipedia.org/w=
/index.php?title=3DApollo_11&amp;action=3Dedit" href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/w/index.php?title=3DApollo_11&amp;action=3Dedit">[update]</a></sup>, =
the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser_Ranging_Retroflector" cl=
ass=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Laser Ranging Retroflector">Lunar Laser Rangin=
g experiment</a> remains operational.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-264" class=3D"refe=
rence"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-264"><s=
pan class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>262<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span>=
</a></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Moonwalk_camera">Moonwalk c=
amera</h3></div>
<p>The Hasselblad camera used during the moonwalk was thought to be lost or=
 left on the Moon's surface.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-265" class=3D"reference"><a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-265"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>263<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup=
>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Lunar_Module_Eagle_memorabi=
lia">Lunar Module <i>Eagle</i> memorabilia</h3></div>
<p>In 2015, after Armstrong died in 2012, his widow contacted the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Air_and_Space_Museum" title=3D"N=
ational Air and Space Museum">National Air and Space Museum</a> to inform t=
hem she had found a white cloth bag in one of Armstrong's closets. The bag =
contained various items, which should have been left behind in the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Module_Eagle" title=3D"Lunar Module=
 Eagle">Lunar Module <i>Eagle</i></a>, including the 16mm Data Acquisition =
Camera that had been used to capture images of the first Moon landing.<sup =
id=3D"cite_ref-266" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-266"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>264<spa=
n class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-267" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-267"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>265<span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
]</span></a></sup> The camera is currently on display at the National Air a=
nd Space Museum.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-268" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-268"><span class=3D"cite-bra=
cket">[</span>266<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id=3D"Anniversary_events">Anniver=
sary events</h3></div>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
1353705441"><div role=3D"note" class=3D"hatnote navigation-not-searchable">=
Further information: <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11_ann=
iversaries" title=3D"Apollo 11 anniversaries">Apollo 11 anniversaries</a></=
div>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id=3D"40th_anniversary"><span id=
=3D"40th_anniversary_events"></span>40th anniversary</h4></div>
<figure class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File/Thumb"><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_Command_Module_in_Hangar.jpg" class=
=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia=
/commons/thumb/3/39/Apollo_11_Command_Module_in_Hangar.jpg/250px-Apollo_11_=
Command_Module_in_Hangar.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"250" height=3D"16=
8" class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"5259" data-file-height=3D"3=
544"></a><figcaption><i>Columbia</i> at the Mary Baker Engen Restoration Ha=
ngar</figcaption></figure>
<p>On July 15, 2009, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life_(magazin=
e)" title=3D"Life (magazine)">Life.com</a> released a photo gallery of prev=
iously unpublished photos of the astronauts taken by <i>Life</i> photograph=
er <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Morse" title=3D"Ralph Mor=
se">Ralph Morse</a> prior to the Apollo 11 launch.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-269" =
class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite=
_note-269"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>267<span class=3D"cite-brac=
ket">]</span></a></sup> From July 16 to 24, 2009, NASA streamed the origina=
l mission audio on its website in real time 40 years to the minute after th=
e events occurred.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-270" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-270"><span class=3D"cite-b=
racket">[</span>268<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> It is in=
 the process of restoring the video footage and has released a preview of k=
ey moments.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-271" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-271"><span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
>[</span>269<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> In July 2010, a=
ir-to-ground voice recordings and film footage shot in Mission Control duri=
ng the Apollo 11 powered descent and landing was re-synchronized and releas=
ed for the first time.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-272" class=3D"reference"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-272"><span class=3D"c=
ite-bracket">[</span>270<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> The=
 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_F._Kennedy_Presidential_Libr=
ary_and_Museum" title=3D"John F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum">J=
ohn F. Kennedy Presidential Library and Museum</a> set up an <a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Flash" title=3D"Adobe Flash">Adobe Flash</=
a> website that rebroadcasts the transmissions of Apollo 11 from launch to =
landing on the Moon.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-273" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-273"><span class=3D"cite=
-bracket">[</span>271<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>On July 20, 2009, Armstrong, Aldrin, and Collins met with President =
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barack_Obama" title=3D"Barack Obam=
a">Barack Obama</a> at the White House.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-274" class=3D"re=
ference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-274">=
<span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>272<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</spa=
n></a></sup> "We expect that there is, as we speak, another generation of k=
ids out there who are looking up at the sky and are going to be the next Ar=
mstrong, Collins, and Aldrin", Obama said. "We want to make sure that NASA =
is going to be there for them when they want to take their journey."<sup id=
=3D"cite_ref-275" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Apollo_11#cite_note-275"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>273<span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> On August 7, 2009, an act of Cong=
ress awarded the three astronauts a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Congressional_Gold_Medal" title=3D"Congressional Gold Medal">Congressiona=
l Gold Medal</a>, the highest civilian award in the United States. The bill=
 was sponsored by Florida Senator <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Bill_Nelson_(politician)" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Bill Nelson (polit=
ician)">Bill Nelson</a> and Florida Representative <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Grayson" title=3D"Alan Grayson">Alan Grayson</a>.<sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-276" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-276"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>274<sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-277" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-277"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>275<span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>A group of British scientists interviewed as part of the anniversary=
 events reflected on the significance of the Moon landing:
</p>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
1244412712"><blockquote class=3D"templatequote"><p>It was carried out in a =
technically brilliant way with risks taken&nbsp;... that would be inconceiv=
able in the risk-averse world of today&nbsp;... The Apollo programme is arg=
uably the greatest technical achievement of mankind to date&nbsp;... nothin=
g since Apollo has come close [to] the excitement that was generated by tho=
se astronauts=E2=80=94Armstrong, Aldrin and the 10 others who followed them=
.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-278" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-278"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>2=
76<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup></p></blockquote>
<div class=3D"mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id=3D"50th_anniversary">50th anni=
versary</h4></div>
<link rel=3D"mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href=3D"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r=
1353705441"><div role=3D"note" class=3D"hatnote navigation-not-searchable">=
Further information: <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11_50t=
h_Anniversary_commemorative_coins" title=3D"Apollo 11 50th Anniversary comm=
emorative coins">Apollo 11 50th Anniversary commemorative coins</a></div>
<p>In June 2015, Congressman <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_=
Posey" title=3D"Bill Posey">Bill Posey</a> introduced resolution H.R. 2726 =
to the 114th session of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United=
_States_House_of_Representatives" title=3D"United States House of Represent=
atives">United States House of Representatives</a> directing the <a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Mint" title=3D"United States M=
int">United States Mint</a> to design and sell commemorative coins in gold,=
 silver and clad for the 50th anniversary of the Apollo 11 mission. On Janu=
ary 24, 2019, the Mint released the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Apollo_11_Fiftieth_Anniversary_commemorative_coins" class=3D"mw-redirect"=
 title=3D"Apollo 11 Fiftieth Anniversary commemorative coins">Apollo 11 Fif=
tieth Anniversary commemorative coins</a> to the public on its website.<sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-279" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-279"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>277<sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-280" class=
=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note=
-280"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>278<span class=3D"cite-bracket">=
]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>A documentary film, <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apol=
lo_11_(2019_film)" title=3D"Apollo 11 (2019 film)">Apollo 11</a></i>, with =
restored footage of the 1969 event, premiered in <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/IMAX" title=3D"IMAX">IMAX</a> on March 1, 2019, and broadly =
in theaters on March 8.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-281" class=3D"reference"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-281"><span class=3D"c=
ite-bracket">[</span>279<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup=
 id=3D"cite_ref-282" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-282"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>280<sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>The Smithsonian Institute's <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/National_Air_and_Space_Museum" title=3D"National Air and Space Museum">Nat=
ional Air and Space Museum</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/NASA" title=3D"NASA">NASA</a> sponsored the "Apollo 50 Festival" on the <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Mall" title=3D"National Mal=
l">National Mall</a> in Washington DC. The three-day (July 18 to 20, 2019) =
outdoor festival featured hands-on exhibits and activities, live performanc=
es, and speakers such as <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Sava=
ge" title=3D"Adam Savage">Adam Savage</a> and NASA scientists.<sup id=3D"ci=
te_ref-283" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ap=
ollo_11#cite_note-283"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>281<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<figure class=3D"mw-default-size" typeof=3D"mw:File/Thumb"><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_projected_on_the_washington_monumen=
t.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.o=
rg/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Apollo_11_projected_on_the_washington_monum=
ent.jpg/250px-Apollo_11_projected_on_the_washington_monument.jpg" decoding=
=3D"async" width=3D"190" height=3D"285" style=3D"--mw-file-upright: 0.75" c=
lass=3D"mw-file-element mw-file-upright" data-file-width=3D"3532" data-file=
-height=3D"5298"></a><figcaption>A Saturn V rocket projected onto the <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Monument" title=3D"Washingto=
n Monument">Washington Monument</a> during the Apollo 11 50th anniversary s=
how</figcaption></figure>
<p>As part of the festival, a projection of the 363-foot (111&nbsp;m) tall =
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturn_V" title=3D"Saturn V">Satur=
n V</a> rocket was displayed on the east face of the 555-foot (169&nbsp;m) =
tall <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Monument" title=3D=
"Washington Monument">Washington Monument</a> from July 16 to the 20th from=
 9:30&nbsp;pm until 11:30&nbsp;pm (EDT). The program  included a 17-minute =
show that combined full-motion video projected on the Washington Monument t=
o recreate the assembly and launch of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Saturn_V" title=3D"Saturn V">Saturn V</a> rocket.<sup id=3D"cite_re=
f-Apollo_50_Go_For_the_Moon_284-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-Apollo_50_Go_For_the_Moon-284"><sp=
an class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>282<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span><=
/a></sup>
</p><p>The projection was joined by a 40-foot (12&nbsp;m) wide recreation o=
f the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kennedy_Space_Center" title=
=3D"Kennedy Space Center">Kennedy Space Center</a> countdown clock and two =
large video screens showing archival footage to recreate the time leading u=
p to the moon landing. There were three shows per night on July 19=E2=80=93=
20, with the last show on Saturday, delayed slightly so the portion where A=
rmstrong first set foot on the Moon would happen exactly 50 years to the se=
cond after the actual event.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Apollo_50_Go_For_the_Moon_2=
84-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_1=
1#cite_note-Apollo_50_Go_For_the_Moon-284"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</=
span>282<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>On July 19, 2019, the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Googl=
e_Doodle" title=3D"Google Doodle">Google Doodle</a> paid tribute to the Apo=
llo 11 Moon landing, complete with a link to an animated YouTube video with=
 voiceover by astronaut <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Co=
llins_(astronaut)" title=3D"Michael Collins (astronaut)">Michael Collins</a=
>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-285" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-285"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>=
283<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-286" =
class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite=
_note-286"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>284<span class=3D"cite-brac=
ket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Aldrin, Collins, and Armstrong's sons were hosted by President <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump" title=3D"Donald Trump">Do=
nald Trump</a> in the Oval Office.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-287" class=3D"referen=
ce"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-287"><span=
 class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>285<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a=
></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-288" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_11#cite_note-288"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</=
span>286<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
